	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-05T17:32:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡟⠀⠀⠀",
				70,
				25
			],
			"Message": "feat(Rest): Implement Phase 3 advanced build features\n\nThis commit adds significant build tooling capabilities to the Rest element for the Land project's VSCode-compatible build pipeline.\n\n## New Modules Added\n\n### Bundle System (`Source/Fn/Bundle/`)\n- `BundleBuilder`: Orchestrates the bundling process with support for single-file, multi-file, and watch modes\n- `BundleConfig`: Comprehensive configuration for bundler (output, minification, tree-shaking, source maps, externals)\n- `EsbuildWrapper`: Optional integration for complex builds that Rest can't handle alone\n\n### NLS Processing (`Source/Fn/NLS/`)\n- `NLSExtractor`: Extracts localization keys from TypeScript source (supports nls.localize, localize, localize2 patterns)\n- `NLSBundle`: Generates and manages localization bundles for different languages\n- `NLSReplacer`: Replaces NLS keys with actual localized strings at build time\n\n### Worker Compilation (`Source/Fn/Worker/`)\n- `WorkerDetector`: Detects worker files by naming conventions and content markers\n- `WorkerBootstrap`: Generates bootstrap code for module, classic, and shared workers\n- `WorkerCompiler`: Orchestrates worker compilation with dependency extraction\n\n### Transform System (`Source/Fn/Transform/`)\n- `PrivateFieldTransform`: Converts TypeScript private fields (#field) to regular properties (__field) for VSCode compatibility\n\n### Advanced Compiler Config (`Source/Struct/CompilerConfig.rs`)\n- Consolidates all Phase 3 feature configurations (NLS, Worker, Bundle)\n- Supports multiple compilation modes: SingleFile, Bundle, Worker, VSCode\n\n## Existing File Updates\n- `Source/Struct/SWC.rs`: Added ModuleFormat enum, TreeShaking, Minify support; updated default target to ES2024\n- `Cargo.toml`: Added `tempfile` workspace dependency for worker compilation tests\n\nThese features enable the Rest element to perform full VSCode build pipeline operations, bundling VS Code platform code from Dependency submodules for use by the Cocoon extension host.",
			"SHA": "028923579dbe498d2cf9ea3ca803aa125b9d39ae"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-04T04:27:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				51,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(deps): Update Rest to use workspace dependencies\n\n- Convert all hardcoded versions to workspace references\n- Available workspace dependencies: anyhow, chrono, clap, dashmap,\n  futures, git2, globset, itertools, notify, num_cpus, par-core,\n  regex, serde, serde_json, swc_*, tokio, tracing, tracing-subscriber,\n  unbug, walkdir\n- Keep rayon as hardcoded (not in workspace)\n\nAddresses DEP-005: Rest workspace reference standardization",
			"SHA": "7ab9a14551f36802ba56db8ed4f4787a402063ae"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T10:04:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				51,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Rest): Update Rust dependencies to latest versions\n\nThis commit updates multiple Rust dependencies in the Rest build tooling element to their latest stable versions. Key updates include:\n\n- **Build dependencies**: `toml` 0.9.11 → 1.0.3\n- **Core utilities**: `anyhow`, `chrono`, `regex` (patch updates)\n- **SWC ecosystem**: Major version bumps across `swc_*` packages (e.g., `swc_ecma_parser` 33.0.1 → 35.0.0, `swc_ecma_transforms_typescript` 40.0.0 → 42.0.0)\n- **Other**: `clap`, `futures`, `git2`\n\nThe Rest element is critical for bundling VS Code platform code from Dependency submodules for use by the Cocoon extension host. Updating these dependencies ensures compatibility with upstream libraries and improves build performance and stability.",
			"SHA": "a01cb9a35f3118b3df55ba34b1d122bf014a6c53"
